Gems are an in-game currency used to buy [[Brawlers]] and their skins, as well as [[XP Doubler]]s, [[Pins]], [[Sprays]], [[Profile Icons]], [[Coins]], and [[Power Points]]. Gems can be purchased with real money either in the in-game Shop or in the Supercell Store, and various other in-game methods.

==Sources==
*Unlocking tiers in the [[Brawl Pass]]. Currently, the Brawl Pass contains 5 tiers that award 10 Gems each, for a total of 50 Gems. Purchasing the Brawl Pass and the Brawl Pass Plus each awards an additional 50 and 100 Gems.
*Unlocking tiers in the [[Pro Pass]]. Currently, the free Pro Pass contains 10 tiers that award 5 Gems each, for a total of 50 Gems. Purchasing the paid Pro Pass awards an additional 600 Gems through several tiers that award 5 Gems and 10 Gems.
*The [[Daily Streak]]. Currently, the 60-day cycle of rewards have 2 days (located at days 5 and 19) that award 3 Gems each, for a total of 6 Gems per 60 days.
*[[Trophy Boxes]] also have a chance of awarding either 3 Gems or 100 Gems in each draw. Bigger Trophy Boxes have a higher chance of awarding a greater number of Gems.
*Purchasing through In-App Purchases or through the Supercell Store. The exact prices of various Gem packages can be found later in this page.
**Purchases through the {{Link|Supercell Store}} provides 10% more Gems when compared with purchases made inside the app.
**The Supercell Store also offers 10 free Gems each Brawl Pass season without spending real money, and 5 free Gems through the daily gifts.
*Supercell also occasionally hosts giveaway contests that award Gems.
*Through some Event Boxes and Event Drops.

==Uses==
*Buying [[XP Doubler]]s from the Shop to double the amount of [[XP]] earned while completing Quests. The doubler costs 25 Gems and doubles the next 1000 XPs received through Quests.
*Purchasing the individual tiers in the Brawl Pass for 30 Gems. The Brawl Pass itself rewards a total of 50 Gems each season on the free side of the pass. An additional 50 Gems is awarded for purchasing the Brawl Pass and 100 additional Gems are awarded for purchasing the Brawl Pass Plus.
*Purchasing the individual tiers in the Pro Pass for 30 Gems. The Pro Pass itself rewards a total of 50 Gems each season on the free side of the pass. An additional 600 Gems is awarded for purchasing the paid Pro Pass.
*Buying [[Coins|Coin]] packs from the Shop.
*Buying [[Power Points]] from the Shop. These appear as offers and can be used on any Brawler.
*Purchasing [[Brawler]] skins offers from the Shop. 
*Purchasing [[Brawler]]s directly. Gems can also be used to top off [[Credits]] used on the Brawler Blast, with one Gem being equivalent to 5.4 to 5.5 Credits depending on Rarity.
*Purchasing Hypercharge Collector's Packs or individual Hypercharges for Brawlers within 7 days when they are first released.
*Changing a player name for 60 Gems. The first name change is free. Any changes after that will cost 30 Gems more. The duration between one name change and another is 3 days.
*Topping up missing Power Points or Coins for upgrading a Brawler. One Gem is equivalent to 10 Coins or 10 Power Points.
*Topping up missing Coins for the purchase of a Gadget, Star Power, Gear, Hypercharge, or True skin. One Gem is equivalent to 10 Coins.
*Topping up missing [[Bling]] for the purchase of an [[Oddities Shop]] offer. One Gem is equivalent to 33 Bling.
*Purchasing exclusive Season Event items and offers, such as [[Monster Eggs]] or [[Brawl Boxes|Mega Boxes]].

